The legal texts and the data about them come from Legimonaco:

  Source : Legimonaco, base de données juridique officielle de la Principauté de Monaco (Gouvernement Princier),
  https://legimonaco.mc

Under the law of Monaco on the protection of literary and artistic works (Loi n° 491 du 24 novembre 1948, article
38), "Les lois, ordonnances, arrêtés, décisions et publications administratives, judiciaires ou officielles ne
bénéficient pas de la protection instituée par la présente loi." The Constitution and the
laws in this repository are texts of that kind. legimonaco.mc publishes no terms of reuse of its own; the terms of
other government sites (journaldemonaco.gouv.mc, gouv.mc) reserve rights in their site content. Only the words of the
law are reproduced here; Legimonaco's editorial notes and its "Historique de consolidation" texts are not reproduced,
except where a version itself prints such a note in the body of an article.

Changes made by Lexifina: each consolidated version's HTML was converted to one Markdown file per article (one line
per paragraph or list item); histories, editorial notes, division headings and page furniture were left out; spacing
was collapsed; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the acts that made each change. The wording
of the law was not changed. Legimonaco and the Gouvernement Princier do not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
